=== DESIGN ===
Goal: Build the Tesla Fleet Telemetry subscription JSON body from protomodel.Signals.

Files:
  - intervals.go: categoryDefaults table (12 categories) + fieldOverrides map + IntervalFor(field).
    - setting_unit=1, driving/location/powertrain=5, charging=10, climate/safety_security/vehicle_state=30, media/config/prefs/metadata=60.
    - Per-field overrides with cited rationale: VehicleSpeed=1, Gear=1, BatteryLevel=30.
    - IntervalFor: returns (interval, true) for known Field; (0, false) for unknown name.
  - config.go: Builder{Hostname, Port}; NewBuilder; SubscriptionFields() []FieldEntry;
    BuildSubscription() ([]byte, error); BuildFor(vins []string) ([]byte, error).
    - Skips Category=="metadata" entries (Unknown/Deprecated_*/Experimental_*).
    - Sorts Fields alphabetically before emit; sorts VINs alphabetically; defensive copy of input slice.
    - Renders text/template; round-trips through encoding/json.MarshalIndent for byte-stable output and validation.
    - No HTTP imports; client_fleet_telemetry.go owns delivery.
  - templates/full_subscription.json.tmpl: Go text/template producing the {vins, config{hostname, port, fields}} shape with custom json func for safe escaping.

Determinism plan:
  - Iterate protomodel.Signals (a deterministic []SignalMeta) instead of map.
  - sort.Slice the FieldEntry list by Name.
  - sort.Strings the VIN copy.
  - json.MarshalIndent sorts map keys alphabetically.
  - => byte-stable output for fixed input.

Coverage test plan:
  - Iterate protomodel.Signals reflectively. For every entry with Category != "metadata", assert it appears in the parsed subscription with a positive interval_seconds. Failure message includes the missing Field name.
  - Iterate protomodel.SignalsByName for IsSettingUnit==true entries; assert interval_seconds == 1 (ADR-004 #4 pinned independently of the categoryDefaults["setting_unit"] entry).
  - TestSubscriptionDeterministic asserts byte-equality across two BuildSubscription calls AND across two BuildFor calls with the same VINs in different orders.
  - TestBuildForIncludesVINs sanity-checks hostname/port/VINs round-trip.
  - TestIntervalForKnownAndUnknownFields exercises override path + unknown-field guard.

